## Workflow

Company standard (plugin `workflow@dev-workflow`). The `/workflow:*` skills follow these values for this project.

- Default branch: `<main>`
- Protected branches: `<main, develop>` - never push directly
- Branch naming: `<type/TICKET-slug>`
- Commit format: `<Conventional Commits: type(scope): summary, footer Refs: TICKET>`
- PR description: `<path to PR template, or "standard /workflow:dev body">`
- Solution docs: `<docs/solutions/>`
- Quality bar: `<docs/quality-bar.md, or "none">`

`/workflow:dev path/to/prd.md` runs the whole flow, pausing for approval after each stage:
clarify → solution doc and test cases (or diagnose for a bug) → branch check and plan → build → test → review → commit → PR.
Each of `/workflow:clarify`, `/workflow:diagnose`, `/workflow:review`, and `/workflow:pr` also works on its own.
Run `/workflow:dev` with no input to resume, or `/workflow:dev commit` / `/workflow:dev pr` to jump to a stage.

Hooks block force push, direct push to protected branches, and edits to `.env` files.

